---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ryan Pégoud"
  description="Research engineer working on inference efficiency, model compression, and GPU kernels."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
    <header>
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-medium text-ink">Ryan Pégoud</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Research Engineer — RL, Knowledge Distillation, GPU kernels
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">
        Montpellier, France{" · "}<a
          href="mailto:ryan.pegoud@outlook.com"
          class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
          >ryan.pegoud@outlook.com</a
        >{" · "}<a
          href="https://github.com/RPegoud"
          class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
          >GitHub</a
        >{" · "}<a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-pegoud"
          class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
          >LinkedIn</a
        >
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-accent">
        Open to research engineer roles in London.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/cv/ryan-pegoud-cv.pdf"
        class="mt-5 inline-block rounded border border-rule px-3 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"
      >
        Download CV ↓
      </a>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-ink-muted uppercase">
        About
      </h2>
      <div
        class="mt-4 space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink"
      >
        <p>
          I'm a research engineer working on inference efficiency and model
          compression, with a background in reinforcement learning. I completed
          an <strong>MSc</strong> in Computational Statistics and Machine Learning
          at <strong>UCL</strong> (Distinction), where my thesis "neural memory augmentation
          for in-context learning in agentic language models" was supervised by <strong
            >Tim Rocktäschel</strong
          >. I also hold an <strong>MEng</strong> in computer engineering.
        </p>
        <p>
          Recently, I was a Visiting Researcher at <strong>BMW Group</strong>,
          where my work focused on white-box knowledge distillation of reasoning
          VLAs for autonomous driving.
        </p>
        <p>
          I write about GPU kernels and reinforcement learning on this site and
          on <strong>Towards Data Science</strong>. My articles on Triton, JAX,
          and transformers have been read over 100,000 times and picked up
          multiple Editor's Picks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-ink-muted uppercase">
        Publications
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-4">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Conference Papers</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.6] text-ink">
          Ryan Sullivan, <strong>Ryan Pégoud</strong>, Ameen Ur Rehman, Xinchen
          Yang, Junyun Huang, Aayush Verma, Nistha Mitra, John P. Dickerson. <a
            href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.11318"
            class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
            >"Syllabus: Portable Curricula for Reinforcement Learning Agents"</a
          >. <em>Reinforcement Learning Conference</em> (RLC), 2025.
          <span class="text-ink-muted">
            <strong>Outstanding Paper Award</strong> — Tooling, Environments, and
            Evaluation for RL.</span
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Workshop Papers</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.6] text-ink">
          <strong>Ryan Pégoud</strong>, Thibault Lahire. <a
            href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tnvVJ_gDVDgdMymbpaT7ClvtTT5tu4bL/view?usp=sharing"
            class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
            >"Better Gradient Steps for Deep On-Policy Reinforcement Learning"</a
          >. <em
            >Aligning Reinforcement Learning Experimentalists and Theorists
            Workshop</em
          >, ICML, 2024.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Writing</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.6] text-ink">
          12 technical articles on Towards Data Science and Data Science
          Collective, covering RL, NLP, JAX, Transformers, Triton, and GPU
          programming — 100k+ reads and multiple Editor's Picks. A selection is <a
            href="/blog"
            class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
            >featured on this site</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">Open Source</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.6] text-ink">
          Multi-agent learning curricula (PyTorch) for <a
            href="https://github.com/RyanNavillus/Syllabus"
            class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
            >Syllabus</a
          >, the curriculum-learning library behind the RLC 2025 paper above; a
          Rainbow DQN implementation (Hessel et al., 2017) for <a
            href="https://github.com/EdanToledo/Stoix"
            class="text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 hover:decoration-accent"
            >Stoix</a
          >, a JAX-based single-agent RL library.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
